  "title": "Singapore: Bio-Engineering Works at Bishan-Ang Mo Kio Park to Prevent Urban Flooding",
  "summary": "This C40 case study describes “Singapore: Bio-Engineering Works at Bishan-Ang Mo Kio Park to Prevent Urban Flooding,” an urban initiative documented for Singapore. It is included because it addresses river flood hazards, and it has evidence relevant to children's livelihoods, and it is located in the Global South. C40 describes the action this way: Previously a concrete canal, the Kallang River was transformed into a naturalized river with bioengineered river edges that meanders through the park…",
